{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1183308-do-garou-go-in-heat","id":1183308,"title":"Do Garou go in heat?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-07T10:59:43-08:00","id":1183308,"title":"Do Garou go in heat?","content":"It might sound like a weird question, but are there any sources detailing how heat or menstruation works for Garou?<br /> My storyteller guesses it would just depend on breed form, with homid garou getting their period every month, and lupus garou going into heat once a year. But afaik, the W20 mentions how incredibly fertile Garou-Garou matings are in producing metis, which wouldn't make sense if all lupus could only receive once a year, anyway. There is the chance that lupus females would only be willing during heat, of course, but there are many animals who mate even when pregnancy is no option, so it stands to reason that a species that is half-human would, too.<br /> Also, it would be incredibly annoying for e.g. felid Ceilican, considering cats keep going into heat every few weeks if they don't mate...<br /> <br /> My guess would be that the Garou would either be somewhere in-between human and wolves, or unlike either, e.g. be fertile year-round with no noticeable heat season. The latter would explain why Garou-Garou works so well, as unlike humans/wolves, they already can conceive whenever they want. It would also solve the problem of not going into heat/not getting your period due to stress, since Garou don't exactly live relaxed lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13143-kalu-chan","name":"Kalu-chan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T11:01:55-08:00","id":1183309,"title":"","content":"Garou females are always fertile.<br /> Excluding period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T11:21:19-08:00","id":1183320,"title":"","content":"IIRC, it's one of the things that wolf-born Garou have to adjust to after the first change. <br /> <br /> (I rather wish there'd been a book - Animal Attraction or something like that - detailing everything about Garou and Fera sex and reproduction, as well as how to use romance and personal relations in chronicles, various romance genre tropes, and the like.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T11:31:01-08:00","id":1183324,"title":"","content":"&quot;Well cub, its time to give you the Corax and Ananasi talk&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""