4)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T16:32:40-08:00","id":1183756,"title":"","content":"My first instinct would be to say it depends on the form you're in, maybe influenced by your breed, so if a homid stays in her lupus form for months at a time, she might not ovulate every month, whereas if a lupus stays in her homid form for months at a time, she might ovulate every month. But if it's covered in the Changing Ways material, I'd yield to that as the authority.<br /> <br /> By the way, I hope I'm not the only one who thought of replying with the question, &quot;Does a Gurahl poop in the woods?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}